                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To exempt from (often military) duty because of injury or ill health."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e2e650f-4f02-4cfd-b807-caf163b36a45",
                                                "sense_id": "e5e95203-34d2-3bb2-b832-522ffd7fdc8c",
                                                "text": "He was invalided home after the car crash."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4473f34-d46b-4b7d-bf82-6a77cebac9f5",
                                                "sense_id": "e5e95203-34d2-3bb2-b832-522ffd7fdc8c",
                                                "text": "Blackadder: Right, Baldrick, this is an old trick I picked up in the Sudan. We tell HQ that I’ve gone insane, and I’ll be invalided back to Blighty before you can say \"wibble\" — a poor, gormless idiot."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91296006-1125-4a65-bf3c-e1f1c695238f",
                                                "sense_id": "e5e95203-34d2-3bb2-b832-522ffd7fdc8c",
                                                "text": "The Japanese armored cruiser Nisshin has been hit badly. Shells have sheared off several main guns and virtually disarmed the vessel. In the middle of all this, one Ensign Isoroku Yamamoto loses two fingers to the remains of an explosion. If he'd lost a third, he would've been invalided out of military service. Thus, by the retention of a single digit would there be rather large consequences a few decades later on down the line."
                                            }
                                        ]
